# Animation performance

- Prefer **transform** and **opacity**. Avoid animating layout (top/left/width/height) and heavy filters on large layers.
- One orchestrated cinematic moment > many competing loops.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`; keep meaning without flourishes.
- Cancel timelines / rAF / Motion subscriptions on unmount or route exit.
- Reuse existing CSS (`--oneb-intro-*`) and `framer-motion` before proposing new libraries.
- GSAP + @gsap/react are installed. Do not install Rive or other animation runtimes unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never animate one element with both GSAP and framer-motion; pause GSAP idle loops when the hub pane is inactive.
- After non-trivial motion changes, treat **Xcode / physical iPhone** (`npm run build:ios` when user says `ios`) as the performance gate.
- Follow `cinematic-motion-graphics` and `gsap-performance` for deeper guidance.
